WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:01.880
Hey there, welcome to 3Blue1Brown.

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:04.100
So, I make videos that animate math.

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:08.040
For a lot of them, I just try to find something kinda interesting or thought provoking,

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:12.360
not necessarily in the typical progression of subjects that a student would see in school.

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:15.340
To see what I mean there, check out some of the Recommended playlist.

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:18.340
Some of the channel, though, is more directly targeted at people

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:21.000
actually trying to learn a commonly taught subject.

00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:25.769
For an example of what I mean there, check out the Essence of Linear Algebra series that I did.

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:30.480
I'll always be working on some other 'Essence of' series like this, so stay posted for more.

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:36.360
Now, when I say that these videos animate math, on the one hand, I mean that very directly;

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:40.940
things are explained with moving visuals and anthropomorphic kinda-cartoonish pi creatures,

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:46.600
but my hope here is that they animate math in another, more literal sense of giving life to the subject.

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:50.440
Math kinda gets a bad rap for being abstruse and inhuman,

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:55.500
and let's face it, a lot of it is symbol heavy and can be introduced in a pretty unmotivated way.

00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:59.120
But the fact is, good math is nothing less than art.

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:01.700
I'm guessing a lot of you out there know that feeling

00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:04.220
when you wrap your mind around a really clever argument

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:07.560
and it's got that very unique flavour of satisfaction.

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:12.460
And same goes for re-understanding something familiar, but in a novel or unexpected light.

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:16.820
Here, I'm just trying to do my part to share feelings like those with more people.

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:19.360
So take a look at some of the videos here,

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:21.760
and if you want to stay posted about new stuff,

00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:25.380
or to just see new videos rather than this trailer whenever you come back to the page,

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:27.200
consider subscribing.

